From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 06:11:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 51/51] compositor: don't cull with actors that clip what they
 paint

A shell can clip a window actor to one monitor while the window reaches
past it, such as a column of a scrolling layout that peeks out at a
monitor edge shared with another monitor. Culling took the window's
opaque region as covering the part the clip hides, so the windows and
the wallpaper underneath stopped being drawn there and the area showed
garbage.

Actors with a clip are now left out of culling, like actors with
effects: they paint fully and hide nothing below them.
---
 src/compositor/meta-cullable.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/compositor/meta-cullable.c b/src/compositor/meta-cullable.c
index 6e55809ec62a3c38d389f4215bd16497cbc73bf2..ad6e22d4ac20b533762bfe2df44810d49924de77 100644
--- a/src/compositor/meta-cullable.c
+++ b/src/compositor/meta-cullable.c
@@ -118,6 +118,11 @@ cull_out_children_common (MetaCullable    *cullable,
       if (needs_culling && has_active_effects (child))
         needs_culling = FALSE;
 
+      /* A clip hides parts of the actor that its opaque region still
+       * claims to cover, so it can't tell what it obscures either. */
+      if (needs_culling && clutter_actor_has_clip (child))
+        needs_culling = FALSE;
+
       if (needs_culling)
         {
           g_autoptr (MtkRegion) actor_region = NULL;
